  "summary": "Charlotte residents met with Flock Safety representatives as CMPD prepares to select an ALPR vendor by an October 5 bid deadline. The debate is shadowed by two recent local officer misuse cases\u2014CMPD Officer Seth Elliott and Mooresville Officer Elizabeth Snowman\u2014both charged with unauthorized Flock database queries, alongside state-level expansion of ALPR authority in North Carolina.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The North Carolina State Bureau of Investigation arrested Officer Seth Daniel Elliott on July 29 and charged him with misdemeanor illegal access of a computer after he allegedly queried Flock Safety and state CJLEADS databases to leak an undercover officer's vehicle details to a suspected drug target in Watauga County",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Mooresville Police Officer Elizabeth Snowman was arrested on August 5 and charged with accessing computers after an internal audit revealed she allegedly performed 31 unauthorized Flock database searches to track her boyfriend's ex-wife",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "The department has maintained inter-agency data-sharing agreements that enabled officers to conduct more than 4,600 queries into Flock camera networks owned by other North Carolina municipalities",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
